1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,816
Last time, the ruin could talk.

2
00:00:02,266 --> 00:00:03,940
Today, it keeps a secret.

3
00:00:04,840 --> 00:00:08,364
A crew that listens at the door gets one more answer further in.

4
00:00:09,264 --> 00:00:11,247
That answer opens a side room,

5
00:00:11,697 --> 00:00:13,670
and a small story of its own.

6
00:00:15,470 --> 00:00:17,367
And when they find what's in the room,

7
00:00:17,817 --> 00:00:19,685
the main screen stops being a window,

8
00:00:20,135 --> 00:00:22,518
and becomes a film, for ten seconds.

9
00:00:23,718 --> 00:00:26,959
A clue is something the crew learns in one place

10
00:00:27,409 --> 00:00:29,587
that changes what happens in another.

11
00:00:30,487 --> 00:00:31,753
You've already written one,

12
00:00:32,203 --> 00:00:34,488
when Mark the Gallery put a place on the map.

13
00:00:35,388 --> 00:00:37,561
Today there are two new words.

14
00:00:38,461 --> 00:00:41,915
Learn, on an answer, writes a word down for this crew.

15
00:00:42,365 --> 00:00:45,312
And learned, on another answer, counts the words.

16
00:00:47,112 --> 00:00:48,177
It can count them,

17
00:00:48,627 --> 00:00:51,177
or it can ask for one word by name.

18
00:00:52,077 --> 00:00:55,287
What's learned in a call goes on one list, for the whole game.

19
00:00:56,187 --> 00:00:58,188
And here's the rule that shapes everything:

20
00:00:58,638 --> 00:01:02,577
the game reads the count when the crew opens the scene, and only then.

21
00:01:03,477 --> 00:01:05,241
If they open a call too early,

22
00:01:05,691 --> 00:01:07,853
going away and coming back doesn't help.

23
00:01:08,753 --> 00:01:11,589
So the clue has to come first on the road.

24
00:01:12,789 --> 00:01:14,573
Every ship flies through the ring,

25
00:01:15,023 --> 00:01:16,832
so the first clue goes there.

26
00:01:17,732 --> 00:01:20,421
It takes a place, on the same spot as the ring,

27
00:01:20,871 --> 00:01:23,169
with a role of its own, plate.

28
00:01:24,069 --> 00:01:26,122
It takes a beat, the same as last time:

29
00:01:26,572 --> 00:01:29,566
when a ship is within five hundred of the plate, Rook calls.

30
00:01:30,466 --> 00:01:33,715
And it takes the scene, with one take and two answers.

31
00:01:35,515 --> 00:01:36,569
Here's the new part.

32
00:01:37,019 --> 00:01:39,370
After Log the names there's a semicolon,

33
00:01:39,820 --> 00:01:41,310
and then learn names.

34
00:01:42,210 --> 00:01:45,116
Names is my word, and the crew never sees it.

35
00:01:45,566 --> 00:01:47,486
What they see is Log the names.

36
00:01:48,686 --> 00:01:50,711
Now the altar gets one new answer,

37
00:01:51,161 --> 00:01:53,125
between the two that are there.

38
00:01:54,026 --> 00:01:56,449
It says play the entry keyed to Dace,

39
00:01:56,899 --> 00:01:59,412
and after the round brackets comes a condition:

40
00:01:59,862 --> 00:02:01,938
if learned is at least one.

41
00:02:02,838 --> 00:02:05,717
So a crew that knows nothing gets two answers,

42
00:02:06,167 --> 00:02:09,214
and a crew that logged the names gets three.

43
00:02:11,014 --> 00:02:13,176
The answer leads to a new scene.

44
00:02:14,076 --> 00:02:15,189
It has one take:

45
00:02:15,639 --> 00:02:18,406
Dace didn't come out, and there's a cairn in a side room.

46
00:02:19,306 --> 00:02:23,037
And it has one answer, which leads on to The Rest of It,

47
00:02:23,487 --> 00:02:26,301
so this crew still hears the main recording.

48
00:02:27,501 --> 00:02:29,762
He said a side room, so there has to be one.

49
00:02:30,662 --> 00:02:34,327
It's a chamber, six hundred, with a passage to the Nave,

50
00:02:34,777 --> 00:02:36,087
and that's Lecture 2.

51
00:02:36,987 --> 00:02:40,234
In the middle of it there's a place, with a rock standing on it,

52
00:02:40,684 --> 00:02:42,042
and that's Lecture 3.

53
00:02:43,842 --> 00:02:46,794
Now the answer shows it, with reveal cairn.

54
00:02:47,694 --> 00:02:50,846
That's the key of the place, and not crypt.

55
00:02:51,296 --> 00:02:54,231
A room isn't a place, and lint won't tell you.

56
00:02:55,431 --> 00:02:58,495
A side story is a quest that isn't part of the main story.

57
00:02:59,395 --> 00:03:00,662
It has three hashes.

58
00:03:01,112 --> 00:03:05,385
It starts when revealed, so it's asleep and out of the list.

59
00:03:06,285 --> 00:03:09,610
And it's done when a ship is within four hundred of the cairn.

60
00:03:11,410 --> 00:03:12,748
The description's a page,

61
00:03:13,198 --> 00:03:15,595
so under the first line there's a small table.

62
00:03:16,495 --> 00:03:19,081
It lists five surveyors, and who came out.

63
00:03:19,981 --> 00:03:23,331
The crew only sees this quest after they've heard the names,

64
00:03:23,781 --> 00:03:25,306
so the table can use them.

65
00:03:27,106 --> 00:03:31,278
The answer starts it, with a comma and then accepts stayed.

66
00:03:32,178 --> 00:03:34,880
That's two things after one semicolon.

67
00:03:36,680 --> 00:03:41,228
Now, in the game's shipped ruins you'll find a section called Side Stories,

68
00:03:41,678 --> 00:03:43,644
and those are a different animal.

69
00:03:44,544 --> 00:03:47,766
Each one says For, and a job.

70
00:03:48,216 --> 00:03:49,883
They belong to one person,

71
00:03:50,333 --> 00:03:54,019
and they're handed over when that person leaves the ship in a suit.

72
00:03:54,919 --> 00:03:56,534
So leave that section for now.

73
00:03:56,984 --> 00:04:00,402
You'll type one at the end of the class, in Lecture 10.

74
00:04:01,602 --> 00:04:03,407
A cutscene is a list of shots.

75
00:04:04,307 --> 00:04:07,901
It's a new section, and its key has to be cutscenes.

76
00:04:08,801 --> 00:04:11,346
The first record is the cutscene itself,

77
00:04:11,796 --> 00:04:16,014
with its key, and Letterbox yes for the black bars.

78
00:04:16,914 --> 00:04:19,266
Then there's one record for each shot.

79
00:04:21,066 --> 00:04:23,733
A shot says which cutscene it belongs to.

80
00:04:24,183 --> 00:04:26,003
It says what the camera looks at,

81
00:04:26,453 --> 00:04:29,948
and that's a role, the same word I write after reach.

82
00:04:30,848 --> 00:04:34,149
It says how near: close, medium or wide.

83
00:04:34,599 --> 00:04:38,694
Two words with a comma make a move, from wide to close.

84
00:04:39,594 --> 00:04:41,705
It says how many seconds.

85
00:04:42,605 --> 00:04:46,413
And Overlay, lower third, puts words at the bottom:

86
00:04:46,863 --> 00:04:49,782
a name, and under the fence, the line.

87
00:04:51,582 --> 00:04:54,975
Everywhere else in this file, that line is my own note.

88
00:04:55,425 --> 00:04:56,822
Here, the crew reads it.

89
00:04:57,722 --> 00:05:01,306
So keep the cutscene short, because the crew can't skip it,

90
00:05:01,756 --> 00:05:03,628
and keep each line short too.

91
00:05:04,828 --> 00:05:05,824
I run lint first.

92
00:05:06,724 --> 00:05:10,555
It says nothing in this mission reads a section keyed cutscenes.

93
00:05:11,005 --> 00:05:13,705
It's right, and the end of its sentence is the fix:

94
00:05:14,155 --> 00:05:15,445
add the line that reads it.

95
00:05:17,245 --> 00:05:19,390
That's a card, in two parts.

96
00:05:20,290 --> 00:05:22,390
Part one goes in the map block,

97
00:05:22,840 --> 00:05:24,760
under the line that builds the ruin,

98
00:05:25,210 --> 00:05:26,884
and I don't change a letter of it.

99
00:05:27,784 --> 00:05:28,993
Lint is clean now.

100
00:05:29,443 --> 00:05:32,067
The section is read, and still nothing plays it.

101
00:05:33,867 --> 00:05:35,759
So the quest has to say when,

102
00:05:36,209 --> 00:05:39,526
with Then, signal, cairn found.

103
00:05:40,426 --> 00:05:42,716
That's my word, and lint warns again:

104
00:05:43,166 --> 00:05:45,593
the word is sent, and nothing hears it.

105
00:05:46,493 --> 00:05:49,373
Part two goes at the very end of the story file.

106
00:05:49,823 --> 00:05:54,730
When that word is sent, it plays the cutscene with this key, on every main screen.

107
00:05:55,630 --> 00:05:58,970
Two things in it are mine, the word and the key.

108
00:05:59,420 --> 00:06:00,478
And lint is clean.

109
00:06:01,678 --> 00:06:03,050
Now for three breaks.

110
00:06:03,950 --> 00:06:06,388
First, I turn the sign round,

111
00:06:06,838 --> 00:06:09,728
and lint tells me that it can't read that condition.

112
00:06:10,628 --> 00:06:14,324
That's good, because that answer would never have been offered.

113
00:06:16,124 --> 00:06:19,632
Next, I misspell a subject, and lint says clean.

114
00:06:20,532 --> 00:06:23,101
Lint reads the outside of a cutscene,

115
00:06:23,551 --> 00:06:25,292
and not the inside of a shot.

116
00:06:26,192 --> 00:06:27,785
That shot would be left out,

117
00:06:28,235 --> 00:06:33,426
and the game does say so, in one line, in its log, after you've played.

118
00:06:35,226 --> 00:06:37,463
Last, I misspell the overlay.

119
00:06:37,913 --> 00:06:40,802
It's clean again, and this time nothing says anything:

120
00:06:41,252 --> 00:06:43,110
the shot plays with no words.

121
00:06:44,010 --> 00:06:47,246
There's a table on the page of the ones nothing tells you about.

122
00:06:47,696 --> 00:06:48,854
Read it before you play.

123
00:06:50,054 --> 00:06:53,484
Through the ring we go, and there's Rook, at the ring.

124
00:06:53,934 --> 00:06:55,180
I log the names.

125
00:06:56,080 --> 00:06:58,493
Across the Nave and up the tunnel,

126
00:06:58,943 --> 00:07:01,786
and there's Rook at the altar, with my third answer.

127
00:07:02,686 --> 00:07:05,572
I take the entry for Dace, and I mark the side room.

128
00:07:06,022 --> 00:07:08,486
Then the rest of it, and I mark the Gallery.

129
00:07:10,286 --> 00:07:12,780
There's a new contact on the far side of the Nave,

130
00:07:13,230 --> 00:07:15,536
and a new quest in the list.

131
00:07:16,436 --> 00:07:20,497
So back down, straight across, and into the side room.

132
00:07:22,297 --> 00:07:23,295
And there it goes.

133
00:07:24,195 --> 00:07:25,199
The bars come up.

134
00:07:25,649 --> 00:07:28,576
The altar: the tally on the rim stops at forty-one.

135
00:07:29,476 --> 00:07:33,089
The cairn: forty-one stones, one for each day.

136
00:07:33,989 --> 00:07:35,000
And then we're back.

137
00:07:36,800 --> 00:07:39,472
One thing you'll notice is that panel in the corner.

138
00:07:39,922 --> 00:07:42,578
It says The Altar, energy zero.

139
00:07:43,478 --> 00:07:46,854
It's the ship's own panel, reading whatever the camera is on.

140
00:07:47,304 --> 00:07:49,784
It isn't in my file, and I can't take it away.

141
00:07:50,984 --> 00:07:51,987
Now it's your turn.

142
00:07:52,887 --> 00:07:56,426
Give Rook a line that only a crew who knows will hear.

143
00:07:57,326 --> 00:08:00,183
Pay for the side story, and add a third shot.

144
00:08:01,083 --> 00:08:03,502
Then break one line where lint can see it,

145
00:08:03,952 --> 00:08:05,327
and one where it can't.

146
00:08:07,127 --> 00:08:09,053
Next time, the main story.
